  <h2 id="why-matters">Why this matters</h2>
  <ul class="why-list">
    <li>Chronic visceral fat accelerates brain aging faster than almost any other lifestyle variable in men</li>
    <li>Elevated insulin locks fat-burning off — no amount of calorie restriction overcomes it without addressing the hormonal root</li>
    <li>Microbiome health sits upstream of metabolic regulation — GLP-1 without gut repair is half a protocol</li>
    <li>GLP-1 medications (semaglutide, tirzepatide) are legitimate clinical tools, not shortcuts, when metabolic markers are off</li>
  </ul>

  <MiniTwoPaths otcLabel="Explore the Foundational Stack" otcHref="/assessment" prompt="Ready to act?" />

  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Visceral fat is not inert tissue. It produces inflammatory cytokines — IL-6, TNF-α —
    that cross the blood-brain barrier, accelerate cognitive aging, and suppress hormone
    function in compounding cycles. This is not a cosmetic issue — it is a metabolic and
    cognitive one, and willpower alone has never fixed a hormonal environment.
  </p>
  <p>
    What most GLP-1 weight-loss platforms miss: visceral fat accumulation is downstream
    of microbiome health. A compromised biome degrades insulin signaling, short-chain
    fatty acid production, and bile-acid metabolism — the upstream levers that govern
    whether energy is partitioned into lean tissue or stored as inflammatory visceral
    adipose tissue. The same compromised biome leaks LPS endotoxins into circulation,
    which amplify the inflammatory cytokine load and degrade the blood-brain barrier.
    GLP-1 medication addresses appetite and glycemic control; it does not restore the
    microbiome. Running semaglutide or tirzepatide on top of an unrepaired gut is why so
    many men regain weight the moment the medication stops. Our protocol pairs GLP-1
    therapy with gut restoration (Biome NS Ultra / BPC-157) so the metabolic environment is
    actually rebuilt underneath the weight loss.
  </p>

  <aside class="protein-first-rule">
    <span class="protein-first-tag">Universal Rule — Especially on GLP-1</span>
    <h2>30g Protein-First, Every Feeding Window</h2>
    <p>The most-missed rule in GLP-1 weight loss: when total intake drops, lean mass becomes the variable most at risk. <strong>Open every feeding window with 30g+ lean protein, 30 minutes before any other food.</strong> This is the leucine-signal threshold that triggers maximal muscle protein synthesis — non-negotiable for protecting lean mass through the satiety drop. Lean mass is what drives the visceral-fat reduction we actually want.</p>
  </aside>

